(1512425, 200586, 35044, '<td valign="top">frame uneven is very distracting.  fruit interesting, but central compostion is static, and surely the point is colour!  And kiwi and orange are not necessarily the best combination, in that the scene feels false.</td>', 'frame uneven is very distracting.  fruit interesting, but central compostion is static, and surely the point is colour!  And kiwi and orange are not necessarily the best combination, in that the scene feels false.', '2005-07-06 14:04:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1512428, 200442, 24454, '<td valign="top">What great execution on this photo.   I had something like this in mind, but never got it implemented.  You have represented my idea very well!   Good luck!</td>', 'What great execution on this photo.   I had something like this in mind, but never got it implemented.  You have represented my idea very well!   Good luck!', '2005-07-06 14:05:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1512431, 199138, 3080, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you''ve heard it already, but you may want to turn the date feature off on your cam.  It adds nothing to the image and I guarantee you wont be selling any images with the date stamp blaring from the side of the image.  The least that can be done is crop the thing out if you can''t figure how to turn it off.<br/>Second, your image is kind of small.  250x375 pixels.  You''re allowed to submit up to a 640x640 image, take advantage of that.  Otherwise, we can''t really see the details in your image to  help you out much.<br/>That being said, your focus looks soft on the subject.   We are not getting much detail out of the little guy at all.  The blurred leaf is a huge distraction as it takes up most of the photo.  The shadow from the blurry leaf in the front takes up another great portion of the photo and engulfs it in darkness.    Did you use flash?  I think attention would be drawn better to the subject without the shadows, without the huge blurry leaf and had the image been bigger.  Maybe crop closer to the eye with a larger image?  ~Heather~</td>', 'I''m sure you''ve heard it already, but you may want to turn the date feature off on your cam.  It adds nothing to the image and I guarantee you wont be selling any images with the date stamp blaring from the side of the image.  The least that can be done is crop the thing out if you can''t figure how to turn it off.Second, your image is kind of small.  250x375 pixels.  You''re allowed to submit up to a 640x640 image, take advantage of that.  Otherwise, we can''t really see the details in your image to  help you out much.That being said, your focus looks soft on the subject.   We are not getting much detail out of the little guy at all.  The blurred leaf is a huge distraction as it takes up most of the photo.  The shadow from the blurry leaf in the front takes up another great portion of the photo and engulfs it in darkness.    Did you use flash?  I think attention would be drawn better to the subject without the shadows, without the huge blurry leaf and had the image been bigger.  Maybe crop closer to the eye with a larger image?  ~Heather~', '2005-07-06 14:05:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1512432, 200737, 35804, '<td valign="top">Excellent! LOOOOOVE the warm vintage tones...gorgeous soft lighting...and the DOF is very pleasing...going into my favorites right now...</td>', 'Excellent! LOOOOOVE the warm vintage tones...gorgeous soft lighting...and the DOF is very pleasing...going into my favorites right now...', '2005-07-06 14:05:43.000000', NULL, 1),
