(1532365, 199835, 39850, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the helpful comments and beneficial feedback.<br/> <br/>For the record, the first time I saw another ''ant'' picture was in this challenge (although surprised to see it <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=200567" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">(''Social Circle'')</a>, for me it was still a different concept).  I conceded then my idea wasn''t as original as I thought.  When I saw <i>"..i saw the same shot on.."</i>, I thought that I was going to see MY photo at that link.  The <a href="//www.photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=2495344" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> referred photo</a> I saw was indeed similar to my ''pre-pp'' image, but it was the first time I had ever seen it.  It was also the first time I ever saw the <a href="//www.photo.net/photodb/photo?photo_id=1672189" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"> original to THAT photo </a> (read the comments there if you are interested).  <br/> <br/>I concede the idea is not that novel now, but I did before that delusion was shattered ":)".  All part of the ''learning''.<br/> <br/>Here are some of the ''finalists'' for my entry.  My better half (who it seems was right, as usual) preferred the sharper angle, but I wanted to ensure it looked like a <b>CIRCLE</b>.  <br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/orig/247812.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/orig/247812.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/orig/247812.jpg"/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=247811" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247811.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247811.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247811.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I chose the one I did because I liked the angle best and I liked how the ants out of focus created a ''blurred border''.  I also liked the two ants in the foreground.  For me ''the subject'' was the actual circle, not the ants.<br/> <br/>The original before ''pp'':<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=247809" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247809.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247809.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/39850/thumb/247809.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>PS: My Icelandic is a little rusty.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-10-23 01:26:49.</i></td>', 'Thank you for the helpful comments and beneficial feedback. For the record, the first time I saw another ''ant'' picture was in this challenge (although surprised to see it (''Social Circle''), for me it was still a different concept).  I conceded then my idea wasn''t as original as I thought.  When I saw "..i saw the same shot on..", I thought that I was going to see MY photo at that link.  The  referred photo I saw was indeed similar to my ''pre-pp'' image, but it was the first time I had ever seen it.  It was also the first time I ever saw the  original to THAT photo  (read the comments there if you are interested).   I concede the idea is not that novel now, but I did before that delusion was shattered ":)".  All part of the ''learning''. Here are some of the ''finalists'' for my entry.  My better half (who it seems was right, as usual) preferred the sharper angle, but I wanted to ensure it looked like a CIRCLE.      I chose the one I did because I liked the angle best and I liked how the ants out of focus created a ''blurred border''.  I also liked the two ants in the foreground.  For me ''the subject'' was the actual circle, not the ants. The original before ''pp'':  PS: My Icelandic is a little rusty.', '2005-07-13 09:42:58.000000', '2005-10-23 02:26:49.000000', 0),
