(1532438, 198464, 39549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by shadow:</b></div><hr/><i> For this contest everyone who has the word circle in their title is getting a max 10 score. This is a copy and paste version that I am including in every photo that I upgrade to 10 due to the title. We as members of DPchallenge need to be reminded of the topic of the challenge  we really need to reread the topic every time we reach a photo. If circle is in the title and it is appropriate I will give a 10. I am sorry if you do not agree with my method of voting   but scores are all I have. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Keeping to theme is of course key, but having circle in the title is zero indication that it meets the theme. It will punish good photos with bad themes and reward blindly. <br/> <br/>But as to this photo, fantastic. Beautiful model, great depth of field, solid composition.</td>', 'Originally posted by shadow: For this contest everyone who has the word circle in their title is getting a max 10 score. This is a copy and paste version that I am including in every photo that I upgrade to 10 due to the title. We as members of DPchallenge need to be reminded of the topic of the challenge  we really need to reread the topic every time we reach a photo. If circle is in the title and it is appropriate I will give a 10. I am sorry if you do not agree with my method of voting   but scores are all I have.   Keeping to theme is of course key, but having circle in the title is zero indication that it meets the theme. It will punish good photos with bad themes and reward blindly.  But as to this photo, fantastic. Beautiful model, great depth of field, solid composition.', '2005-07-13 10:10:26.000000', NULL, 0),
