(1533029, 199501, 14671, '<td valign="top">Great shot.  The brightness vs. contrast is a little overpowering.  perhaps a -5 (to -10) brightness and +5 (to +10) on contrast would have corrected it.  Well lit and very crisp.</td>', 'Great shot.  The brightness vs. contrast is a little overpowering.  perhaps a -5 (to -10) brightness and +5 (to +10) on contrast would have corrected it.  Well lit and very crisp.', '2005-07-13 14:12:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1533214, 200557, 15832, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beagleboy:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks like a straight-on photo of a display on a computer monitor to me.  Maybe it''s not the case, but it sure looks like it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There is a littel area in Reykjavík (Grafarvog) with this all kind of metal things! kinda art. I placed my camera inside one of those thing and shot this picture in negative, from a low angel in a special prespetiv. Alot of peopel think this is a shot from a monitor but it´s NOT! I´m never gonna take a picture of a picture in a monitor!<br/>It looks excatly like this orginal. just a littel darker</td>', 'Originally posted by Beagleboy: Looks like a straight-on photo of a display on a computer monitor to me.  Maybe it''s not the case, but it sure looks like it.   There is a littel area in Reykjavík (Grafarvog) with this all kind of metal things! kinda art. I placed my camera inside one of those thing and shot this picture in negative, from a low angel in a special prespetiv. Alot of peopel think this is a shot from a monitor but it´s NOT! I´m never gonna take a picture of a picture in a monitor!It looks excatly like this orginal. just a littel darker', '2005-07-13 15:23:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1533231, 199176, 39634, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by art-inept:</b></div><hr/><i> great idea! but maybe shooting from below the hoop and towards the shooter might have added a more dynamic perspective :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That was actually my first idea. I tried this for several shots. I just could not get the sky to work with me, the ball was coming out as a black circle showing no detail.</td>', 'Originally posted by art-inept: great idea! but maybe shooting from below the hoop and towards the shooter might have added a more dynamic perspective :)   That was actually my first idea. I tried this for several shots. I just could not get the sky to work with me, the ball was coming out as a black circle showing no detail.', '2005-07-13 15:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1533232, 199176, 39634, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sukuriant:</b></div><hr/><i> Phenominal timing on that pic; I''d crop the image a little differently, either showing more of the outside, or just enough so that we know it''s a basketball hoop.  How many shots did it take you to catch it right THEN! ...? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>more than 50! =)</td>', 'Originally posted by sukuriant: Phenominal timing on that pic; I''d crop the image a little differently, either showing more of the outside, or just enough so that we know it''s a basketball hoop.  How many shots did it take you to catch it right THEN! ...?   more than 50! =)', '2005-07-13 15:37:33.000000', NULL, 0),
